9.4 Platform checklist
Before leaving this chapter, demonstrate that you can:
• change symbol;
• change timeframe;
• display bid and ask where supported;
• place market orders;
• place buy/sell limits;
• place buy/sell stops;
• add and modify a stop loss;
• add and modify a take profit;
• close a position;
• cancel a pending order;
• view balance/equity/margin;
• locate contract size;
• locate swap/financing terms;
• export or save trade history;
• take chart screenshots;
• set the correct time zone reference in your journal.
9.5 Demo-account setup
Use a realistic virtual balance. If you expect to begin micro-live with a small account later, do not practice
on a USD 1,000,000 demo balance. A realistic balance makes position-sizing behaviour meaningful.
Set your training risk policy from the beginning:
• 0.5% maximum planned risk per simulated trade once you begin strategy exercises;
• <=1.5% simultaneous initial open risk;
• no martingale;
• no widening stops;
• no oversized “just for fun” demo trades.
Your habits on demo should be habits you would trust with real money.
9.6 Exercise: platform competence test
Without referring to a tutorial while doing it:
1. Open EUR/USD H1.
2. Add a horizontal line.
3. Place a pending order far enough away that it is unlikely to execute.
