Chapter 25
Chapter 24 - AUD, CAD, NZD and
CHF: Commodity, Small-Open-Economy
and Safe-Haven Dynamics
25.1 Learning objectives
You should understand why smaller developed-market currencies can be sensitive to commodities,
China/global growth, terms of trade, risk sentiment and local policy.
25.2 Australian dollar (AUD)
Australia is a commodity-exporting economy with significant trade exposure to Asia, including China.
AUD analysis often considers:
• RBA policy expectations;
• inflation and labour data;
• iron ore/commodity conditions;
• Chinese growth and demand;
• global risk sentiment.
Oﬀicial source: RBA Education - Monetary Policy
25.3 Canadian dollar (CAD)
Canada is a major commodity exporter, particularly energy. CAD can be influenced by:
• Bank of Canada policy;
• Canadian/U.S. growth differences;
• oil prices and terms of trade;
• North American trade;
• risk sentiment.
Oﬀicial learning: Bank of Canada Explainers
