Chapter 58
Chapter 57 - Performance Metrics That
Matter
58.1 Learning objectives
You should be able to calculate and interpret a core strategy scorecard while resisting headline-metric
obsession.
58.2 Minimum scorecard
Track:
• trade count;
• win rate;
• average win R;
• average loss R;
• expectancy R/trade;
• net expectancy after costs;
• profit factor;
• maximum drawdown % and R;
• longest losing streak;
• average holding period;
• cost/trade;
• cost as % of gross profit;
• pair contribution;
• year/regime contribution;
• long/short contribution;
• rule adherence in forward/live phases.
58.3 Sharpe ratio - useful but limited
A simplified Sharpe ratio compares excess return with return volatility. It can help compare risk-adjusted
results, but its interpretation depends on sampling, return distribution, autocorrelation and selection bias.
