Chapter 62
Chapter 61 - FOMO, Revenge Trading,
Overtrading and Strategy Hopping
62.1 Learning objectives
You should identify four common behavioural failure loops and implement prewritten interruptions.
62.2 FOMO loop
1. price moves without you;
2. you feel excluded;
3. you enter late without a valid setup;
4. risk/reward worsens;
5. loss creates frustration;
6. another impulsive trade follows.
Countermeasure: a missed valid trade is logged as a missed trade , not chased. The next opportunity
begins from zero.
62.3 Revenge trading loop
1. loss occurs;
2. trader feels need to recover now;
3. size/frequency increases;
4. decisions deteriorate;
5. losses compound.
Countermeasure: fixed post-loss pause and daily/process kill switch.
62.4 Overtrading
More trades are not automatically more opportunity. A trader may lower standards simply to feel active.
Measure trades that met the rules versus trades taken.
