Chapter 62 - Pre-Trade Commitment
and Decision Hygiene
63.1 Learning objectives
You should be able to create a pre-trade record that locks the key decision variables before money or
simulated P/L starts changing your judgment.
63.2 Minimum pre-trade commitment
Before placing an order record:
• strategy/version;
• pair;
• date/time;
• long/short;
• market regime/context;
• exact setup conditions;
• entry and order type;
• initial stop;
• stop distance;
• planned exit;
• account equity;
• risk %;
• cash risk;
• calculated position size;
• total/cluster risk after the trade;
• scheduled-news check;
• invalidation;
• screenshot;
• emotion scores.
If you cannot write the trade clearly, you do not have permission to enter.
