Chapter 66
Chapter 65 - Weekly, Monthly and
Quarterly Review
66.1 Learning objectives
You should be able to separate routine review from strategy redesign and use predetermined metrics rather
than mood.
66.2 Weekly review
Review:
• every trade;
• missed valid trades;
• invalid trades taken;
• total R;
• net cost;
• rule adherence;
• emotion patterns;
• open-risk violations;
• upcoming macro calendar;
• one process improvement.
Do not redesign a strategy every weekend.
66.3 Monthly review
Add:
• rolling expectancy;
• profit factor;
• max drawdown;
• pair/session contribution;
• long/short contribution;
