Chapter 67
Chapter 66 - Demo Trading as Forward
Testing, Not a Game
67.1 Learning objectives
You should understand the purpose and limitations of demo trading, set demo conditions that resemble
intended live trading and distinguish strategy evidence from simulated execution convenience.
67.2 What demo can test
Demo trading can test:
• whether signals can be recognized in real time;
• whether your routine fits your schedule;
• whether you follow the rulebook without future bars;
• how the strategy behaves through current market conditions;
• whether the journal/review system works;
• whether historical assumptions resemble forward observations.
67.3 What demo cannot fully test
Demo cannot perfectly reproduce:
• emotional response to real money;
• all live slippage/latency;
• every liquidity condition;
• withdrawal/custody concerns;
• the temptation created by meaningful gains/losses.
That is why micro-live exists later.
67.4 Make demo realistic
Use:
197

Forex Trading From First Principles to Advanced Practice Version 1.0
• a balance broadly relevant to your intended starting capital;
• intended risk policy;
• realistic leverage settings where configurable;
• only the instruments in Strategy A;
• normal working hours;
• no balance resets after losses;
• no giant experimental lots inside the serious account.
If you want to experiment, use a separate sandbox demo. Keep the serious forward-test account
clean.
67.5 Minimum demo gate
The reference framework requires at least:
• 100 valid demo trades ;
• >=95% rule adherence ;
• positive net expectancy;
• no catastrophic drawdown;
• 30 consecutive trades without unauthorized changes;
• reasonable agreement between demo behaviour and tested assumptions.
If Strategy A is slow and 100 trades require longer than the calendar, wait. Do not manufacture trades.
67.6 Exercises
1. Create a serious demo account with a realistic balance.
2. Write its starting equity and risk rules on page 1 of the journal.
3. Separate sandbox experimentation from oﬀicial forward-test trades.
4. Define the exact fields that will be compared with backtest assumptions.
67.7 Quiz 66
1. What can demo test well?
2. What can demo not fully reproduce?
3. Why use a realistic demo balance?
4. Why avoid resetting after losses?
5. What is the minimum trade count in the course gate?
6. What happens if the strategy needs 18 months to generate 100 valid trades?
