Chapter 68
Chapter 67 - The 100-Trade
Forward-Test Protocol
68.1 Learning objectives
You should be able to execute a formal forward test, create checkpoints without changing rules prematurely
and make a go/no-go decision from evidence.
68.2 Before Trade 1
Freeze:
• Strategy A version;
• eligible pairs;
• risk model;
• broker/demo venue;
• expected cost assumptions;
• news rule;
• journal fields;
• review triggers;
• no-go conditions.
68.3 Checkpoints
68.3.1 Trades 1-25
Focus on execution mechanics. Do not infer profitability from the sample. Fix journal/process bugs, but
strategy-rule changes require a new test.
68.3.2 Trades 26-50
Review adherence, costs and whether signals are being interpreted consistently.
