70.5 No strategy changes because “money feels different”
If you are unable to execute the frozen rules with real money, reduce size further or return to demo. Do
not solve fear by moving stops or taking profits early.
70.6 Scaling gate
Only consider moving toward 0.5% if:
• at least 25-50 clean live observations exist;
• =95% discipline remains;
• actual costs resemble assumptions;
• drawdown remains within tested expectations;
• no custody/withdrawal concern exists;
• the strategy’s edge still appears intact.
There is no requirement to scale. Staying at 0.25% can be rational.
70.7 Exercises
1. Define the exact maximum cash risk for a hypothetical micro-live account.
2. Create a live-versus-demo execution table.
3. Write three conditions that force a return to demo.
4. Write why “I am profitable after five live trades” is insuﬀicient evidence.
70.8 Quiz 69
1. What is the purpose of micro-live?
2. What risk/trade does the course start with?
3. How many clean live trades precede consideration of scaling?
4. What if minimum lot size forces excess risk?
5. What should happen if real-money fear causes rule violations?
6. Is scaling mandatory?
