Chapter 74
Chapter 73 - Operational Security,
Account Safety and Continuity
74.1 Learning objectives
You should protect access to trading funds, build a simple continuity plan and understand that operational
failure can create financial risk even when the strategy is sound.
74.2 Account security
Use:
• unique strong password;
• multi-factor authentication where available;
• protected email account with its own MF A;
• device lock/encryption;
• no credential sharing;
• verified oﬀicial broker URLs/apps;
• anti-phishing habits.
74.3 Payment security
Funding and withdrawal should use accounts you control and comply with broker ownership/KYC rules.
Be suspicious of requests to send money to personal accounts, crypto wallets or unrelated third parties to
“activate” withdrawals.
74.4 Continuity plan
Write what happens if:
• internet fails;
• phone/laptop fails;
• broker platform is down;
