Chapter 75
Chapter 74 - Scams, Signals, Copy
Trading, Binary Options and
“Guaranteed” Systems
75.1 Learning objectives
You should identify common forex marketing traps and apply a due-diligence standard before paying for
any trading product or service.
75.2 The central filter
If a seller’s business model depends on you believing profits are easy, demand more evidence, not less.
CFTC consumer material warns about forex fraud, unusually high return promises, social-media solicita-
tion and unregistered dealers. Oﬀicial resource: https://www.cftc.gov/LearnAndProtect/forexfrauds
75.3 Red flags
• guaranteed returns;
• “zero risk”;
• fixed daily profit claims;
• pressure to deposit immediately;
• secret strategy that cannot be objectively defined;
• only winning screenshots;
• withdrawal fees paid to a personal/crypto address;
• account management by someone who will not identify a regulated entity;
• fabricated regulator logos;
• remote-access requests to your banking/trading device;
• martingale presented as “recovery”;
• unverifiable audited record.
