Chapter 79
Chapter 78 - Currency Futures and
What They Add to Your Analysis
79.1 Learning objectives
You should understand exchange-traded FX futures, contract standardization, central clearing, open in-
terest and why futures data can provide useful context to an OTC trader.
79.2 Futures structure
Currency futures trade on regulated exchanges with:
• standardized contract size;
• defined expiration months;
• exchange rules;
• central clearing;
• margin requirements;
• exchange-published volume/open interest.
CME’s FX education is a primary learning resource: https://www.cmegroup.com/education/courses/int
roduction-to-fx
79.3 Futures versus retail spot/CFD
Key differences can include:
• centralized exchange versus OTC dealer relationship;
• contract expiry versus typically rolling retail CFD;
• transparent exchange volume/open interest versus broker-specific tick/activity data;
• futures margin rules versus broker retail leverage framework;
• quotation conventions that may differ.
