Chapter 85
Chapter 84 - Advanced Central-Bank
Analysis: Reaction Functions and
Communication
85.1 Learning objectives
You should move beyond the policy-rate decision and interpret central-bank communication as a condi-
tional reaction function.
85.2 Decision is only one data point
Analyze:
• rate decision;
• vote split;
• statement language;
• forecasts/projections;
• press conference;
• balance-sheet policy;
• forward guidance;
• discussion of risks;
• changes relative to prior meeting.
85.3 Reaction function
Build a conditional map:
If inflation remains above target and labour markets stay tight, policy may remain restrictive;
if demand and employment weaken sharply while inflation falls, easing may become more likely.
The exact map differs across central banks and regimes.
