Chapter 86
Chapter 85 - Fiscal Policy, Sovereign
Risk and Political Economy
86.1 Learning objectives
You should understand how fiscal policy can affect growth, inflation, yields and currency risk, and why
higher yields are not always bullish.
86.2 Fiscal channels
Government spending/tax policy can affect:
• aggregate demand;
• inflation;
• public borrowing;
• sovereign debt supply;
• growth expectations;
• central-bank reaction;
• investor confidence.
86.3 Higher yield: good or bad?
Yield can rise because:
1. growth expectations improve;
2. central-bank tightening is expected;
3. inflation risk rises;
4. fiscal/credit risk rises.
The first two can support a currency; the last two may undermine it if investors demand compensation
for risk.
