Chapter 91
Chapter 90 - Graduation: The Gate
Before the IT/Systematic Track
91.1 Learning objectives
You should know exactly what knowledge and evidence must exist before programming, automation,
machine learning or Expert Advisors enter the curriculum.
91.2 Why technology remains postponed
Technology can accelerate both good research and bad research. A beginner with optimization software
can search thousands of parameter combinations without understanding why the result is meaningless. A
knowledgeable trader can instead ask a precise falsifiable question.
This course therefore ends the trading-knowledge track before teaching Python/MQL5/ML.
91.3 Knowledge graduation checklist
You must be able to explain, without assistance:
• FX instruments and OTC versus exchange structure;
• bid/ask, spread, pips, lots, margin and leverage;
• order types and execution risks;
• position sizing across major/cross pairs;
• chart structure and volatility;
• indicators as transformations of data;
• central-bank transmission and reaction functions;
• major macro releases and expectation/surprise logic;
• yields, carry, external balances and risk sentiment;
• correlation and portfolio exposure;
• expectancy, R, PF, drawdown and losing streaks;
• strategy specification;
• look-ahead, out-of-sample testing and overfitting;
249

Forex Trading From First Principles to Advanced Practice Version 1.0
• robustness and edge decay;
• behavioural biases and adherence;
• broker due diligence and Kenyan regulatory checks;
• demo/micro-live gates;
• advanced spot/forward/swap/futures/options/COT vocabulary.
91.4 Evidence graduation checklist
Before the IT track you should have:
• =85% foundation and macro exams;
• =90% risk/strategy/process exams;
• 100 annotated charts;
• 20 macro event studies;
• 50+ position-sizing drills with full accuracy after corrections;
• one frozen Strategy A specification;
• roughly 200-300 historical observations where feasible;
• separate out-of-sample evidence;
• robustness report;
• =100 serious demo trades;
• =95% rule adherence;
• 30-trade integrity challenge;
• a professional trading plan.
Micro-live is desirable before automating live execution, but programming can begin after the knowl-
edge/evidence gate if it remains research-only and does not shortcut live-risk controls.
91.5 The question you should be able to ask technology later
Not:
“Find me a profitable forex bot. ”
But:
“Here is Strategy A v1.0, its exact signal timing, cost model and risk rules. Reproduce my
manual backtest, run the predeclared out-of-sample and robustness tests, and report every
assumption without optimizing anything I did not authorize. ”
That is the difference between using IT as leverage and using it as a gambling machine.
