Chapter 117
Appendix Y - Gate Exam Answer
Framework
Gate exams include open-ended explanations and practical submissions. The goal is not to memorize one
sentence. Use the following scoring rubric.
117.1 Gate A - Market Mechanics
Pass only if you can:
• explain FX instruments/OTC structure clearly;
• calculate pips/cross logic;
• distinguish bid/ask and order types;
• explain leverage versus risk;
• operate a demo platform;
• verify current CMA sources;
• score >=85% without guessing.
Any confusion that could cause an accidental oversized order is an automatic remediation item.
117.2 Gate B - Chart and Technical Literacy
Pass only if:
• 100 charts are annotated without future information;
• structure labels are consistent;
• support/resistance and breakout definitions are explicit;
• indicators are explained mathematically/conceptually rather than mystically;
• multiple timeframes are used according to defined roles;
• exam >=85%.
117.3 Gate C - Macro
Pass only if:
321

Forex Trading From First Principles to Advanced Practice Version 1.0
• four weekly macro sheets exist;
• at least 20 event studies exist;
• you explain actual versus expectation versus revision;
• you can trace policy -> yields -> FX scenarios;
• you use primary oﬀicial sources;
• exam >=85%.
117.4 Gate D - Risk
Pass only if:
• position sizing is 100% accurate after corrections;
• expectancy, PF, R and drawdown are understood;
• course risk limits are memorized;
• correlated exposure and all-in costs are calculated;
• exam >=90%.
117.5 Gate E - Strategy and Evidence
Pass only if:
• Strategy A is frozen/versioned;
• historical test includes all valid signals;
• roughly 200-300 observations exist where feasible or a defensible slow-system alternative sample exists;
• realistic costs are included;
